<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tun Abdul Majid</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tun Abdul Majid was the Bendahara, or chief minister, of the Johor-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riau">Riau</a> sultanate who became the first of the hereditary Bendahara rulers of Pahang. Around 1770 the sultan granted him Pahang as a fief, and his descendants governed it from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pekan">Pekan</a> as Raja Bendahara. After the Johor-Riau realm broke up in the early 19th century they became effectively independent, and in 1882 his descendant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-muadzam-shah-of-pahang">Wan Ahmad</a> took the title of sultan.</p></div>
